ntdll: Prefer high addresses for Windows top-down allocations on arm64 macOS.

The arm64 loader reserves only the low PAGEZERO area. Searching reserved
areas first puts FEX's large allocator reservations immediately above PE
images, exhausting the limited space for nearby generated code. Search
free addresses above 4 GB first for Windows MEM_TOP_DOWN requests, respecting
the caller's bounds and alignment. Retain reserved-area fallback, explicit
address handling and allocations constrained below 4 GB.

Keep Wine's internal mapping policy: moving its native syscall/first-thread
stack to the top of the address space caused posix_spawn to fail with EFAULT
in the M4 test. This policy change belongs at the Windows allocation API.

Regression: tests/x64-fidelity/topdown.c compares an unbounded top-down
allocation against a known available high range and checks low bounds.

